      id: 'r-routing',
      topic: 'Routing & router composition',
      importance: 4,
      thirtySecond: ':params land in req.params (strings — validate), query in req.query (string or array). Routers are mountable mini-apps: app.use(\'/api/v1/users\', usersRouter). mergeParams reads parent params.',
      twoMinute: 'First-registered-wins among matching routes — specific before catch-all. router.param centralizes per-:id loading. app.route(\'/x\').get().post() groups methods. Nested resources: mount a child router at /users/:userId/orders with mergeParams: true. Versioning falls out naturally: freeze v1Router, mount v2Router alongside. Route-level middleware arrays ([validate(schema), authorize, handler]) read as a pipeline declaration.',
      deepDive: 'Express 5 moved to path-to-regexp 8: regex-in-string params ( :id(\\\\d+) ) and unnamed wildcards changed syntax — a migration gotcha. Param values are decodeURIComponent\'d; query parsing is configurable (query parser setting) and extended parsing allows nested objects, which has been a prototype-pollution vector in other parsers — validate query shapes too.',
      followUps: ['How does mergeParams work?', 'Why register specific routes before generic ones?'],
